<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Port Rashid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1972">1972</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Port Rashid is a port in Dubai, named after the ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashid-bin-saeed-al-maktoum">Rashid bin Saeed Al Maktoum</a> and opened in 1972. Built to expand the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>'s traditional role as a regional <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entrepot">entrepot</a>, it was soon overtaken in scale by the deep-water port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebel-ali">Jebel Ali</a>, opened in 1979, and was later turned mainly to cruise and passenger traffic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/port-rashid.jpg" alt="Port Rashid" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Imre Solt · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Port_Rashid_on_1_May_2007_Pict_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
